  <Figure src="/images/screen-shot-2014-08-18-at-09.21.46.png" alt="A page from the Wordsmith non-fiction eBook series." wide />
  <p>Students aged 7-8</p>
  <h3>Tutankhamen</h3>
  <p>“Who Killed Tutankhamen?” was an exciting ePub designed for Year 3 students (aged 7-8) that followed two detectives as they unraveled the mysteries surrounding the life and death of the famous pharaoh. With animated characters, scrolls, and clickable items, young readers explored ancient Egypt and discovered fascinating clues. This interactive adventure helped children understand the history and culture of Tutankhamen’s time while solving the mystery themselves.</p>
  <Figure src="/images/screen-shot-2014-08-18-at-09.27.14.png" alt="A page from the Wordsmith non-fiction eBook series." wide />
  <Figure src="/images/screen-shot-2014-08-18-at-09.28.28.png" alt="A page from the Wordsmith non-fiction eBook series." wide />
  <p>Students aged 9-10</p>
  <h3>Animal migration</h3>
  <p>“Animals on the Move” was designed for Year 5 students (aged 9-10) and explored the incredible migrations of wildebeests, butterflies, salmon, humpback whales, and arctic terns. With videos, fast facts, quizzes, and animated maps, young readers learned about the diverse journeys of these animals across land, sea, and air. I created and animated all the illustrations myself, enhancing the educational experience and helping children appreciate the wonders of animal migration.</p>
